01:57:00.110 --> 01:57:05.060
But I can tell you this, I was Will at one time.

2767
01:57:05.060 --> 01:57:08.130
Where you're out of control and wait,

2768
01:57:08.130 --> 01:57:11.760
all that had to do, that was going on in will.

2769
01:57:11.760 --> 01:57:13.420
Like that was going on in his,

2770
01:57:13.420 --> 01:57:16.390
you saw there was more going on there

2771
01:57:16.390 --> 01:57:18.287
than that joke.
Yeah. Oh, of course.

2772
01:57:18.287 --> 01:57:19.120
(laughs) You know what I mean?

2773
01:57:19.120 --> 01:57:20.004
It was like watching this man-

2774
01:57:20.004 --> 01:57:21.900
I mean, it's like the Zapruder film.

2775
01:57:21.900 --> 01:57:23.170
You could break this thing down,

2776
01:57:23.170 --> 01:57:25.990
you know, look at it.
Haw, that was me!

2777
01:57:25.990 --> 01:57:28.093
All that stuff that's going down.

2778
01:57:28.093 --> 01:57:30.540
I didn't beat that guy down for disrespecting wife.

2779
01:57:30.540 --> 01:57:32.287
It was something else.

2780
01:57:32.287 --> 01:57:34.496
You don't pick a guy up and slam him on his head

2781
01:57:34.496 --> 01:57:37.840
on the concrete for that.

2782
01:57:37.840 --> 01:57:39.187
It was something in me.

2783
01:57:39.187 --> 01:57:41.470
Didn't have anything to do with him.

2784
01:57:41.470 --> 01:57:44.240
And there's many, many times I would just smack people

2785
01:57:44.240 --> 01:57:47.520
and do stuff because I had this inner anger

2786
01:57:47.520 --> 01:57:50.200
that I did not control.

2787
01:57:50.200 --> 01:57:54.900
And it's so vicious and so crazy and insidious.

2788
01:57:54.900 --> 01:57:58.453
And it sneaks up on you at the...

2789
01:57:58.453 --> 01:58:00.370
like I promise you Will did not plan that out.

2790
01:58:00.370 --> 01:58:01.540
Of course not.
Okay?

2791
01:58:01.540 --> 01:58:04.730
It's like going into a blackout.

2792
01:58:04.730 --> 01:58:05.563
Blacked out.

2793
01:58:05.563 --> 01:58:08.497
And you knew when he was like,

2794
01:58:08.497 --> 01:58:12.350
"Get my wife's name out your fucking mouth."

2795
01:58:12.350 --> 01:58:16.250
I mean, we were all like, holy, this dude is lost.

2796
01:58:16.250 --> 01:58:17.860
He's having a meltdown.

2797
01:58:17.860 --> 01:58:20.020
But I knew that guy. That was me.

2798
01:58:20.020 --> 01:58:23.090
You couldn't calm me down after stuff like this.

2799
01:58:23.090 --> 01:58:26.580
And this is where my wife had to come and say, look man,

2800
01:58:26.580 --> 01:58:29.820
if you ever do this, man, and see,

2801
01:58:29.820 --> 01:58:32.540
then I have to tell everybody, 'cause what was wild,

2802
01:58:32.540 --> 01:58:34.630
'cause in my community, in the black community,

2803
01:58:34.630 --> 01:58:36.750
they were like, you should have knocked the guy out.

2804
01:58:36.750 --> 01:58:37.870
Sure.
That's the rule.

2805
01:58:37.870 --> 01:58:41.310
And you know, you're like the prototype alpha.

2806
01:58:41.310 --> 01:58:43.180
How could this happen to you?
You're too big.

2807
01:58:43.180 --> 01:58:45.242
I mean, you do a million takes on this whole thing.

2808
01:58:45.242 --> 01:58:47.860
But can I ask you this,

2809
01:58:47.860 --> 01:58:50.920
would you have believed my story

2810
01:58:50.920 --> 01:58:52.483
had I had knocked the guy out?

2811
01:58:53.370 --> 01:58:54.833
I don't think anybody would.

2812
01:58:56.210 --> 01:58:57.960
I just, you're at a party.

2813
01:58:57.960 --> 01:58:59.530
Terry Crews knocks out the head

2814
01:58:59.530 --> 01:59:03.993
of the Motion Picture Department because he, what?

2815
01:59:05.780 --> 01:59:06.613
Mm-hmm.

2816
01:59:06.613 --> 01:59:08.210
Terry probably had some drinks.

2817
01:59:08.210 --> 01:59:09.043
Yeah.
He probably didn't...

2818
01:59:09.043 --> 01:59:11.810
Listen, I don't drink. They be like, oh no.

2819
01:59:11.810 --> 01:59:12.653
Yeah right.

2820
01:59:13.540 --> 01:59:14.970
Yeah, you just decided,

2821
01:59:14.970 --> 01:59:16.930
maybe they did something you didn't like,

2822
01:59:16.930 --> 01:59:21.090
but there's that mean thug, Terry, we've been waiting on.

2823
01:59:21.090 --> 01:59:23.800
'Cause I got a whole record of you beaten up people.

2824
01:59:23.800 --> 01:59:24.720
Mm-hmm.

2825
01:59:24.720 --> 01:59:28.770
Yeah, conversely, what would've happened had Will Smith

2826
01:59:28.770 --> 01:59:30.587
walked on stage and just said,

2827
01:59:30.587 --> 01:59:31.950
"Hey Chris, you know I love you,

2828
01:59:31.950 --> 01:59:34.302
but that was out of line, you know?"

2829
01:59:34.302 --> 01:59:37.450
And just handled it with composure.

2830
01:59:37.450 --> 01:59:40.810
He would've been this unbelievable hero.

2831
01:59:40.810 --> 01:59:43.260
Imagine if you'd put it in his acceptance speech-

2832
01:59:43.260 --> 01:59:44.223
Right, just waited until then.

2833
01:59:44.223 --> 01:59:46.653
What Chris said about my wife, man,

2834
01:59:47.820 --> 01:59:50.410
you know, it was over the line,

2835
01:59:50.410 --> 01:59:51.840
but I'm here to accept my...

2836
01:59:51.840 --> 01:59:54.220
And it would've been hero.
Right. Right.

2837
01:59:54.220 --> 01:59:56.210
But let me tell you what Hollywood's about,

2838
01:59:56.210 --> 02:00:00.230
and this is where me and Hollywood have always been at odds.

2839
02:00:00.230 --> 02:00:01.820
The head of the motion picture,

2840
02:00:01.820 --> 02:00:04.640
the head of William Morris Endeavor

2841
02:00:04.640 --> 02:00:06.590
told me he could get away with it.

2842
02:00:06.590 --> 02:00:08.720
I had a private meeting with him.

2843
02:00:08.720 --> 02:00:10.260
It's all in the book.

2844
02:00:10.260 --> 02:00:13.440
And I said, "Hey man, you don't get to molest the clients

2845
02:00:13.440 --> 02:00:15.040
and go to work the next day."

2846
02:00:15.040 --> 02:00:17.200
He said, "Yes, he can."

2847
02:00:17.200 --> 02:00:19.200
And he said, "What I'm gonna do is take his title

2848
02:00:19.200 --> 02:00:20.581
and suspend them for 30 days."

2849
02:00:20.581 --> 02:00:23.663
And I said, "Man, hey man, you gonna give him a vacation?

2850
02:00:25.520 --> 02:00:26.420
What are you talking about?

2851
02:00:26.420 --> 02:00:29.180
You can't molest the clients.

2852
02:00:29.180 --> 02:00:31.100
What are you doing?"

2853
02:00:31.100 --> 02:00:33.753
It was the same as the standing ovation for Will.

2854
02:00:35.020 --> 02:00:38.020
And I went, I said, "Dude, what are you talking about?"

2855
02:00:38.020 --> 02:00:39.490
I handed him a letter.

2856
02:00:39.490 --> 02:00:42.210
I grabbed his letter that he wrote

2857
02:00:42.210 --> 02:00:45.630
demanding that Mel Gibson be kicked out of Hollywood.

2858
02:00:45.630 --> 02:00:48.560
He wrote it for The Huffington Post for antisemitic remarks.

2859
02:00:48.560 --> 02:00:50.900
I said, "Look, you said, Mel Gibson

2860
02:00:50.900 --> 02:00:53.510
needs to be kicked out of Hollywood forever

2861
02:00:53.510 --> 02:00:54.380
for these remarks.

2862
02:00:54.380 --> 02:00:57.690
But antisemitic remarks, as reprehensible as they are,

2863
02:00:57.690 --> 02:00:59.620
they are not illegal.

2864
02:00:59.620 --> 02:01:02.053
What your man did is a crime.

2865
02:01:03.040 --> 02:01:06.020
And you're telling me it's different?"

2866
02:01:06.020 --> 02:01:08.597
He said, "It's different, Terry."

2867
02:01:10.410 --> 02:01:11.810
I couldn't believe it, dude.

2868
02:01:13.860 --> 02:01:15.740
I just said, and that's the rules.

2869
02:01:15.740 --> 02:01:19.110
See the rules of Hollywood is

2870
02:01:19.110 --> 02:01:21.835
call it out until it happens to you. (laughs)

2871
02:01:21.835 --> 02:01:24.370
You know what I mean? Cancel anybody else.

2872
02:01:24.370 --> 02:01:28.210
But us? No, no, not at all.
(Terry claps)

2873
02:01:28.210 --> 02:01:29.170
'Cause we meant well.

2874
02:01:29.170 --> 02:01:31.080
Right, well, and then you pursue,

2875
02:01:31.080 --> 02:01:32.930
you file criminal charges,

2876
02:01:32.930 --> 02:01:35.230
even knowing like that's probably not gonna go anywhere,

2877
02:01:35.230 --> 02:01:38.960
and then the civil suit, which ultimately doesn't

2878
02:01:38.960 --> 02:01:41.780
look like it's gonna go anywhere until a couple other dudes

2879
02:01:41.780 --> 02:01:42.970
come out of the woodwork.
That's right.

2880
02:01:42.970 --> 02:01:44.589
And then it's a whole different thing.

2881
02:01:44.589 --> 02:01:46.170
Whole different story.

2882
02:01:46.170 --> 02:01:48.500
And some females.
Mm-hmm.

2883
02:01:48.500 --> 02:01:50.793
Guys and girls. It was crazy.

2884
02:01:52.980 --> 02:01:54.370
But if I hadn't gone public,

2885
02:01:54.370 --> 02:01:59.010
it would've never brought the real people out,

2886
02:01:59.010 --> 02:02:02.730
and they wanted to join my case privately without,

2887
02:02:02.730 --> 02:02:03.937
you know, saying their names and the whole thing,

2888
02:02:03.937 --> 02:02:05.720
and I respected that.

2889
02:02:05.720 --> 02:02:08.060
But the thing was is that they were willing

2890
02:02:08.060 --> 02:02:11.300
to go to the mat for this guy.

2891
02:02:11.300 --> 02:02:16.300
And it was so foul and so corrupt,

2892
02:02:16.350 --> 02:02:17.840
'cause you gotta understand about Hollywood.

2893
02:02:17.840 --> 02:02:21.470
I mean like Harvey Weinstein would lead, you know,

2894
02:02:21.470 --> 02:02:25.810
all these women in Hollywood parties at his house

2895
02:02:25.810 --> 02:02:27.930
while he was raping them.
Mm.

2896
02:02:27.930 --> 02:02:30.830
You know, and this is the thing, you're talking about...

2897
02:02:32.022 --> 02:02:35.880
One reason I wrote the book was that I noticed

2898
02:02:35.880 --> 02:02:38.390
that there was things where success

2899
02:02:38.390 --> 02:02:40.293
is the warmest place to hide.

2900
02:02:41.780 --> 02:02:44.230
You know, it's a great place 'cause you don't,

2901
02:02:44.230 --> 02:02:45.783
no one calls you on your shit.

2902
02:02:46.730 --> 02:02:50.053
No one, because you're the man. You're Will Smith.

2903
02:02:51.530 --> 02:02:54.793
You're the head of the Motion Picture Department.

2904
02:02:57.000 --> 02:03:00.800
And when what we need, 'cause we talk about values,

2905
02:03:00.800 --> 02:03:02.620
we can say values,

2906
02:03:02.620 --> 02:03:06.440
but unless you actually act on those values,

2907
02:03:06.440 --> 02:03:07.670
it means nothing.

2908
02:03:07.670 --> 02:03:09.860
Ultimately money and power rule.

2909
02:03:09.860 --> 02:03:14.520
And in the case of this Adam Bennet thing,

2910
02:03:14.520 --> 02:03:18.080
it wasn't until money and power were threatened

2911
02:03:18.080 --> 02:03:21.110
that you were actually able to move the needle.

2912
02:03:21.110 --> 02:03:25.790
And what's interesting is that typically in these cases,

2913
02:03:25.790 --> 02:03:28.820
then it then becomes about how can we discredit

2914
02:03:28.820 --> 02:03:30.500
the person going after us?
Yeah.

2915
02:03:30.500 --> 02:03:33.980
But because you had done all that inside work

2916
02:03:33.980 --> 02:03:36.530
and kind of owned up publicly and privately

2917
02:03:36.530 --> 02:03:39.563
to the stuff that they would've been able to hang over you-

2918
02:03:39.563 --> 02:03:40.396
Yeah.

2919
02:03:40.396 --> 02:03:41.870
There was a freedom with that, right?

2920
02:03:41.870 --> 02:03:43.823
Where you were like, come at me.

2921
02:03:44.880 --> 02:03:47.860
That was, again,

2922
02:03:47.860 --> 02:03:50.470
when you're talking about gratitude,

2923
02:03:50.470 --> 02:03:54.083
I'm beyond thankful for that D-Day,

2924
02:03:55.200 --> 02:03:59.340
for that moment when I saw myself as I really was,

2925
02:03:59.340 --> 02:04:00.490
because if I hadn't,

2926
02:04:00.490 --> 02:04:03.340
liked you could ask me like, where do you think you'd be?

2927
02:04:04.290 --> 02:04:07.793
Oh my God. You know, running, hiding.

2928
02:04:09.970 --> 02:04:10.803
Imagine.

2929
02:04:10.803 --> 02:04:13.010
I would've had no strength to do anything,

2930
02:04:13.010 --> 02:04:15.960
to even come up against something like that

2931
02:04:15.960 --> 02:04:17.300
had I had secrets like that.

2932
02:04:17.300 --> 02:04:18.930
'Cause they would've found stuff.

2933
02:04:18.930 --> 02:04:20.790
Well and had you not unpacked those secrets,

2934
02:04:20.790 --> 02:04:22.740
you would've cold-cocked the guy.

2935
02:04:22.740 --> 02:04:24.223
Right and then-

2936
02:04:24.223 --> 02:04:25.660
But you might not have even been at that party

2937
02:04:25.660 --> 02:04:28.210
to begin with, but-
See, we can keep going.

2938
02:04:28.210 --> 02:04:29.043
You know what I mean?
(Rich laughs)

2939
02:04:29.043 --> 02:04:31.420
It's kinda like it could have been over before that.

2940
02:04:31.420 --> 02:04:32.520
It could have been...

2941
02:04:32.520 --> 02:04:34.440
But where the question really is

2942
02:04:34.440 --> 02:04:36.203
is where would the fall have come?

2943
02:04:37.530 --> 02:04:38.980
That's really what we're talking about.

2944
02:04:38.980 --> 02:04:42.310
Like what would've taken me out, you know?

2945
02:04:42.310 --> 02:04:45.710
'Cause all of this, any of this deception

2946
02:04:45.710 --> 02:04:48.880
that I was living was going to take me out some way,

2947
02:04:48.880 --> 02:04:50.610
shape or form.
Right.

2948
02:04:50.610 --> 02:04:53.603
And I'm gonna tell you, man,

2949
02:04:55.640 --> 02:04:57.530
that's where gratitude comes in for me right now.

2950
02:04:57.530 --> 02:05:00.490
'Cause I'm just like, oh, if I hadn't have done it,

2951
02:05:00.490 --> 02:05:01.430
I just thank God.

2952
02:05:01.430 --> 02:05:03.470
So I'm just thankful for my wife.

2953
02:05:03.470 --> 02:05:05.113
I'm thankful for my family.

2954
02:05:05.970 --> 02:05:09.330
I'm thankful for the people who did stick with me.

2955
02:05:09.330 --> 02:05:11.960
'Cause it was a very lonely time during that period.

2956
02:05:11.960 --> 02:05:14.670
There were camps and people were like,

2957
02:05:14.670 --> 02:05:16.926
what is Terry talking about?

2958
02:05:16.926 --> 02:05:19.930
And in my own community, I was looked at as a pariah

2959
02:05:19.930 --> 02:05:23.690
for even technically joining Me Too,

2960
02:05:23.690 --> 02:05:27.580
which they thought was a female thing, until all these men.

2961
02:05:27.580 --> 02:05:32.060
I mean we had wrestlers and pro athletes

2962
02:05:32.060 --> 02:05:34.430
that came out about, you know.

2963
02:05:34.430 --> 02:05:38.920
The fact is there's a organization called 1in6

2964
02:05:38.920 --> 02:05:41.630
that talks about one and six men

2965
02:05:41.630 --> 02:05:45.280
have been sexually molested at some time in their life,

2966
02:05:45.280 --> 02:05:47.040
and wait, and don't even acknowledge it.

2967
02:05:47.040 --> 02:05:49.580
Some they've been in military and whatever.

2968
02:05:49.580 --> 02:05:50.610
And they just called it,

2969
02:05:50.610 --> 02:05:54.160
well, the guy was goofing around, but you've been molested.

2970
02:05:54.160 --> 02:05:56.170
Yeah.
That line was crossed.

2971
02:05:56.170 --> 02:05:59.890
And if you don't unpack that and deal with that,

2972
02:05:59.890 --> 02:06:01.573
you're gonna act out in some way

2973
02:06:01.573 --> 02:06:05.260
that is not in service to you or others.

2974
02:06:05.260 --> 02:06:09.890
Prison is full, full of people who were,

2975
02:06:09.890 --> 02:06:13.340
at one time or another, used and abused in that way

2976
02:06:14.200 --> 02:06:15.610
and acted out in some of,

2977
02:06:15.610 --> 02:06:18.133
but would never, ever tell what happened to them.

2978
02:06:19.270 --> 02:06:22.050
And because I mean, that's why, you know,

2979
02:06:22.050 --> 02:06:25.290
you doing what you've done is so powerful

2980
02:06:25.290 --> 02:06:28.920
and palpable because you are cut from this cloth

2981
02:06:28.920 --> 02:06:30.010
of the ultimate, you know,

2982
02:06:30.010 --> 02:06:31.560
you've got this incredible physique

2983
02:06:31.560 --> 02:06:33.624
and this incredible career,

2984
02:06:33.624 --> 02:06:37.710
and as such for you to be able to come to the microphone

2985
02:06:37.710 --> 02:06:40.210
and talk about these things, I think, gives permission

2986
02:06:40.210 --> 02:06:42.930
to all of these people who are harboring

2987
02:06:42.930 --> 02:06:46.223
these stories with shame and in secrecy.

2988
02:06:47.270 --> 02:06:49.270
I'll tell you this, I will say,

2989
02:06:49.270 --> 02:06:52.950
my greatest accomplishment

2990
02:06:52.950 --> 02:06:55.230
beyond film, beyond movies

2991
02:06:55.230 --> 02:06:58.760
and TV and all this stuff, was when I got to team up

2992
02:06:58.760 --> 02:07:03.470
with Amanda Nguyen and she is the founder of Rise,

2993
02:07:03.470 --> 02:07:07.270
which we was all about passing

2994
02:07:07.270 --> 02:07:09.740
the Sexual Assault Survivors' Bill of Rights.

2995
02:07:09.740 --> 02:07:13.580
Because the thing is that whoever the perpetrator is

2996
02:07:13.580 --> 02:07:15.240
has tons of rights.

2997
02:07:15.240 --> 02:07:18.670
And she found that anyone who was a victim

2998
02:07:18.670 --> 02:07:21.924
of these things had no rights at all.

2999
02:07:21.924 --> 02:07:25.570
And I joined up with her and we went to Congress

3000
02:07:26.410 --> 02:07:29.520
and what was wild is that she had always

3001
02:07:29.520 --> 02:07:31.260
brought women there to talk.

3002
02:07:31.260 --> 02:07:35.170
And it was never a big, it never got that much light,

3003
02:07:35.170 --> 02:07:39.530
and by having a man there, it was packed.

3004
02:07:39.530 --> 02:07:43.010
That room was full. It was on CNN.

3005
02:07:43.010 --> 02:07:45.910
It was the highlight, and people were like, wait a minute.

3006
02:07:47.230 --> 02:07:50.547
And I look at that and I could feel the millions

3007
02:07:50.547 --> 02:07:53.891
and millions of people who never got the tell.

3008
02:07:53.891 --> 02:07:57.500
Dude, it was, I don't even how to describe it

3009
02:07:57.500 --> 02:07:59.433
because it's something that,

3010
02:08:00.443 --> 02:08:05.253
it comes with so much shame, you know, societal shame.

3011
02:08:06.830 --> 02:08:09.440
But I said, I have nothing to be ashamed of.

3012
02:08:09.440 --> 02:08:12.480
And I remember this was my log line

3013
02:08:12.480 --> 02:08:16.320
during this whole time, I was like, I will not be shamed.

3014
02:08:16.320 --> 02:08:17.720
I did nothing wrong.

3015
02:08:17.720 --> 02:08:21.380
And I had to repeat that because you feel like,

3016
02:08:21.380 --> 02:08:23.213
